# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [3.5.2] - 2026-08-02

### Fixed
- **Homebrew upgrade verification** - `brew upgrade` now verifies the installed version matches the expected release
  - Previously, `brew upgrade` would report success even when the Homebrew formula hadn't been updated yet
  - Now checks `brew info --json=v2` after upgrade to confirm the version actually changed
  - Displays clear warning when Homebrew formula is out of sync with GitHub release

## [3.5.1] - 2026-07-26

### Security
- **Fix CodeQL `js/shell-command-injection-from-environment` alert** in `--doctor` check
  - Replace `runCommandSafe('sh', ['-c', \`command -v ${command}\`])` with direct execution
  - Absolute paths (e.g. `process.execPath`) are now checked via `fs.existsSync()` — no shell involved
  - Bare command names (`zsh`, `git`) are probed with `runCommandSafe(command, ['--version'], { stdio: 'ignore' })` — `execFileSync` with an argument array, immune to shell metacharacter injection
- **`runCommandSafe` now respects `options.stdio`**
  - When `stdio: 'ignore'` or `'pipe'` is passed, suppresses `🚀 Running:` and `✅/❌` console output
  - Enables silent probing without leaking noise to the user's terminal

## [3.5.0] - 2026-07-26

### Added
- **Intelligent .zshrc Parser** (`zshrcParser.js`) - Complete rewrite of .zshrc handling
  - Section detection: user-pre, managed-block, user-post, third-party integrations
  - Duplicate detection for exports, aliases, functions, PATH entries, plugins, themes
  - Syntax validation: detects orphaned `fi`/`done`/`esac`, unclosed blocks, malformed PATH
  - Third-party integration preservation: Kiro CLI, iTerm2, NVM, Homebrew blocks
  - Settings extraction: theme, plugins (including alias-only from metadata), exports, aliases

- **Smart .zshrc Updates** - Intelligent merging instead of appending
  - Preserves user customizations outside the managed block
  - Automatically cleans duplicates when updating
  - Diff preview mode to see changes before applying
  - Auto-repair of common syntax errors

- **Incremental Configuration Updates**
  - `addPlugin(name)` - Add a single plugin
  - `removePlugin(name)` - Remove a single plugin  
  - `setTheme(name)` - Change theme
  - `cleanDuplicates()` - Remove duplicate entries
  - `repairZshrc()` - Fix syntax errors

- **New CLI Flags** for non-interactive updates
  - `--add-plugin <name>` - Add a plugin
  - `--remove-plugin <name>` - Remove a plugin
  - `--set-theme <name>` - Change theme
  - `--analyze` - Show .zshrc analysis report
  - `--repair` - Auto-fix syntax errors
  - `--clean-duplicates` - Remove duplicates
  - `--help` - Show help with all options

- **New Menu Options**
  - "Update existing configuration" - Add/remove plugins, change theme, clean duplicates
  - "Analyze & repair .zshrc" - View analysis report, preview/apply repairs

- **Enhanced Profile Management**
  - `saveCurrentAsProfile(name)` - Save current config as profile
  - `deleteProfile(name)` - Delete a profile
  - `getProfileInfo(name)` - Get profile details
  - `importProfile(path, name)` - Import profile from file
  - `exportProfile(name, path)` - Export profile to file
  - `compareProfiles(name1, name2)` - Compare two profiles

- **Comprehensive Tests** - 34 new tests for parser and manager

### Changed
- Profile format version bumped to v2 with additional metadata
- Backups now include repair operations
- User content cleaning is more aggressive about removing managed items

### Fixed
- **Duplicate entries** - No more duplicate plugins, aliases, PATH entries, exports
- **Syntax errors** - Orphaned `fi` statements, malformed PATH assignments
- **Content corruption** - Error messages no longer embedded in exports
- **Third-party integrations** - Kiro CLI blocks properly preserved at top/bottom

### Migration Notes
If upgrading from v3.4.x:
1. Run `awesome-lazy-zsh --analyze` to see current .zshrc status
2. Run `awesome-lazy-zsh --repair` to fix any syntax errors
3. The next plugin/theme change will automatically clean duplicates
4. Your user customizations outside the managed block are preserved

## [3.4.5] - 2026-07-26

### Security
- Pin and SHA-256 verify the reviewed Oh My Zsh installer; require Homebrew to be installed separately.
- Require signed exact-release tags for Git self-updates and use `npm ci --ignore-scripts`.
- Pin all GitHub Actions, add CodeQL/CODEOWNERS, verify tag signatures in the release workflow, and generate SBOM/provenance attestations.
- Replace the tap's write-capable `pull_request_target` workflow with protected, manually dispatched bottle publication.

### Fixed
- Use stable Homebrew `opt` paths matching the installed `libexec/src/aliases` layout.
- Preserve user `.zshrc` content atomically, remove duplicate Oh My Zsh initialization, unify backups, and reject symlink replacement explicitly.
- Resume pending services and prevent completed plugins from reappearing after another interruption.
- Install and initialize the Starship binary instead of treating its repository as an Oh My Zsh theme.
- Preserve alias-only and custom plugins in profiles and install missing profile components.
- Keep plugin history for deterministic updates/rollback and stop enabling services at boot when users only request a start.
- Isolate all tests from real user state and remove live Git/npm/Homebrew operations from unit tests.

### Homebrew
- Install locked npm dependencies during formula installation with lifecycle scripts disabled.
- Declare `zsh`, `fzf`, and Starship dependencies, execute Node directly at runtime, and functionally test `--version` on every push and PR.

## [3.4.4] - 2026-07-24

### Security
- **Comprehensive external security audit remediation**
  - Fix Oh My Zsh installer: add `--unattended --keep-zshrc` flags and pass `RUNZSH=no CHSH=no` environment variables
  - Fix z plugin: pin to commit SHA (repo has no tags) instead of non-existent tag
  - Pin all GitHub Actions to full commit SHAs for supply-chain security
  - Fix workflow: add `curl -f` flag, SHA256 format validation, explicit permissions, concurrency protection
  - Rewrite `.zshrc` handling with managed-block approach to preserve user customizations
  - Use atomic writes (temp file + rename) to prevent file corruption
  - Use stable `/opt/homebrew/opt/` symlink paths instead of versioned Cellar paths
  - Unify backup directory at `~/.awesome-lazy-zsh/backups/`
  - Create safety backup before restore operations

### Added
- **SECURITY.md** - Vulnerability reporting policy and security documentation
- **Dependabot configuration** - Automated dependency updates for npm and GitHub Actions
- **CI workflow** - Tests on Node 18/20/22, JavaScript syntax checking, ShellCheck linting, npm audit

### Changed
- Support commit SHA refs (40 hex chars) in plugin/theme URLs, not just tags
- Update `runCommandSafe` to support custom environment variables
- Backups now stored in unified `~/.awesome-lazy-zsh/backups/` directory

### Removed
- Stale v3.1.7 formula from main repo (actual formula is in tap repository)

## [3.4.3] - 2026-07-24

### Security
- **Replace `curl | sh` with download-validate-execute for Oh My Zsh installer**
  - Download installer to secure temp file (no shell interpolation)
  - Validate shebang, file size (5KB–500KB), and content markers before execution
  - Clean up temp files automatically
- **File permission hardening (round 2)**
  - Set `0o600` on all `.zshrc` writes (backup, main write, custom plugin update)
  - Set `0o700` on profiles directory creation
  - Set `0o600` on profile export writes
- **Add confirmation prompt to `hr()` history-eval function**
- **Add security warning for `DOTENV_AUTO` auto-source feature**
- **Remove dead `runCommand` imports** (unsafe shell-string executor no longer used in main app)

## [3.4.2] - 2026-07-24

### Security
- **Comprehensive codebase hardening**
  - Add path traversal and URL validation for custom plugins (HTTPS-only, reject localhost/private IPs/embedded credentials)
  - Pin all external plugin/theme repos to specific release tags with shallow clones
  - Replace predictable temp directory with `mktemp -d` + restrictive permissions
  - Set `0o600` permissions on backup files and state files
  - Add binary/package name validators before shell interpolation
  - Sanitize theme/plugin names before writing to `.zshrc`
  - Harden self-update: verify git remote origin, use `--ignore-scripts` for npm
  - Add download sanity checks (shebang validation, file size bounds) in setup.sh
  - Remove dead code (`serviceManager.js`) with unsafe shell patterns

### Changed
- Track `package-lock.json` in version control for reproducible installs
- README: Add `brew trust` step to Homebrew installation instructions

## [3.4.0] - 2026-07-24

### Added
- **Update Notification** - Interactive self-update prompt on startup
  - Checks GitHub for newer versions (throttled: once per 24 hours)
  - Presents "Yes, update now / No / Skip this version" choices
  - Auto-detects install method (git pull or brew upgrade)
  - "Skip this version" prevents repeated prompts for same release
  - 5-second timeout, graceful degradation on network failure
- **ASCII art banner with version** in the Node.js CLI startup

### Changed
- Removed redundant version/feature text from setup.sh (Node.js CLI now handles the banner)

## [3.3.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Resume Setup** - Checkpoint-based state persistence for interrupted setups
  - Automatically saves progress at each major step (plugin selection, plugin installation, service installation, theme selection)
  - Detects incomplete state on re-launch and offers "Resume previous setup" or "Start fresh"
  - Resumes from exact point of interruption — only installs remaining plugins/services
  - Per-plugin progress tracking during installation (never re-installs what already succeeded)
  - 24-hour staleness expiry — expired state files are auto-discarded
  - Schema-versioned state file at `~/.awesome-lazy-zsh-state.json`
  - Graceful degradation — state I/O failures never crash the setup flow
  - Ctrl+C on resume prompt exits without modifying saved state
- **New module**: `stateManager` — state file read/write/validate/expire utilities

## [3.2.1] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Expanded Tool Installation** - 11 new installable tools:
  - Cloud CLI: AWS CLI, Google Cloud SDK, Azure CLI
  - DevOps: kubectl, Terraform, Ansible, Docker Compose
  - Languages: Python 3, Go, Rust, Java (OpenJDK)
- CLI tools and languages correctly skip the "Start services?" prompt

## [3.2.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Service Installation** - Actual server installation when selecting service plugins
  - Interactive prompt after plugin selection to install real servers
  - Granular multi-select for choosing which services to install
  - Platform auto-detection (Homebrew on macOS, apt/yum on Linux)
  - Pre-installation binary checks (skip already-installed services)
  - Post-install option to start services immediately
  - Progress reporting with final summary
  - Fail-forward strategy (one failure doesn't block others)
- **New modules**: serviceRegistry, platformDetector, serviceInstaller, serviceInstallFlow
- **Property-based tests** - 22 tests covering all correctness properties using fast-check
- **Test infrastructure** - Node.js built-in test runner with fast-check for PBT

### Supported Services (macOS/Linux)
- MongoDB Community Server (`brew tap mongodb/brew && brew install mongodb-community`)
- MySQL Community Server (`brew install mysql`)
- PostgreSQL (`brew install postgresql@14`)
- Redis (`brew install redis`)
- RabbitMQ (`brew install rabbitmq`)
- Elasticsearch (`brew tap elastic/tap && brew install elastic/tap/elasticsearch-full`)
- Memcached (`brew install memcached`)

